## Independent acceptance

### PT-2 disposition / Program amendment

The PR preserves PT2_INCOMPLETE_ACCEPTED_AS_FINAL_EVIDENCE_DISPOSITION rather than rewriting PT-2 as complete.

- cases 03-10 remain NOT_RUN, neither pass nor fail;
- no ten-case generalization or aggregate realistic classification/hallucination/semantic/executable rate is asserted;
- case 02 remains censored at 424846 ms;
- runs 37500000739 and 37509368210 remain zero-product-observation measurement failures;
- no further PT-2 dispatch/harness recovery is authorized.

The USER-approved dependency amendment is incorporated into this substantive PT-3 PR rather than a separate activation/state-sync PR. PT-4 remains gated on PT-3 acceptance/merge.

### Supported causal boundary

The correction does not claim that generation, retrieval or repair caused the observed defect. The raw job did not preserve enough stage evidence to support that claim.

The earliest directly supported gap is the final-output trust contract: an OAC-associated CloudFront origin directly referenced a newly declared S3 bucket while the complete generated HCL supplied no S3 read authorization, yet provider/schema/Terraform CLI validation remained PASS and runtime quality did not expose the omission.

AWS's current CloudFront guidance confirms that OAC request signing does not by itself grant S3 access; CloudFront must have permission to access the S3 origin. The observed case therefore supports this semantic/usability defect independently of Terraform syntax/provider validity.

### Implementation

The implementation stays inside existing responsibilities:
- GeneratedTerraformContractInspector receives a bounded lexical final-HCL omission check;
- EvidenceQualityAssessor consumes that deterministic result;
- EvidenceQualityAssessment adds one bounded persisted reason: CLOUDFRONT_S3_ORIGIN_AUTHORIZATION_MISSING;
- known omission wins as DEGRADED while technical PASS remains unchanged.

No prompt/model/retrieval/corpus/scorer change, extra closure/repair/provider call, evaluator LLM, IAM/runtime/infrastructure change, frontend/PT-4 implementation or new orchestration framework is introduced.

The check is not case/resource-name hardcoded. Tests cover renamed buckets, multiple origins, interpolated references, local aliases, unrelated policies, private ACLs, comments/heredocs and nonaffected/external origins.

### Important bounded semantics

This is correctly documented as omission/declaration detection, not an effective-IAM-policy or deployment validator.

A bound non-empty bucket-policy expression or an explicitly declared alternate read path can prevent this specific MISSING reason even though the inspector does not prove the policy principal/action/condition, public-access-block state, ownership-control compatibility or deployment success. That limitation is acceptable for this PT-3 scope because:
- the independently observed defect had no authorization declaration at all;
- the implementation does not claim policy effectiveness or general semantic correctness;
- editable variables/references remain allowed rather than being falsely rejected;
- the runtime boundary remains CONDITIONAL_ON_EXTRACTED_FACTS.

Therefore passing this omission check alone must never be cited as proof that CloudFront/S3 authorization is effective. Future evidence/UX must preserve that limit.

### Same-job regression

The preserved observed HCL SHA 962ea2b714bee2981b0a3993046dc5a65eeefb6fd05d29f4e7026f6665e16971 is replayed offline. With the production-like UNKNOWN project-decision applicability it now produces:
- technical PASS;
- semantic reason CLOUDFRONT_S3_ORIGIN_AUTHORIZATION_MISSING;
- quality DEGRADED.

This is the intended correction: expose a known semantic omission without pretending the original provider/schema/CLI validation failed and without spending another model call.

### Persistence and final-output placement

VertexAnalysisProvider assesses outcome.finalTerraform(), so the check runs on final post-closure/repair HCL rather than only the initial draft. Existing persistence/API round-trip coverage confirms the new reason survives the established quality storage path. No new repair cycle is triggered.

### Validation reviewed

- controlled pre-correction regression: expected 1 failure, EVIDENCE_BACKED instead of DEGRADED;
- focused offline suite: 63 PASS;
- exact observed-HCL replay: 1 PASS;
- full offline backend package: 517 tests, 0 failures/errors, 2 existing external MariaDB skips;
- frozen realistic-v1 identity: 26 files unchanged;
- original PT-2 artifact identities/censor/attempt counts preserved;
- exact-head Backend Local Verification run 37554777098: SUCCESS;
- exact-head Terraform Static Verification run 37554776979: SUCCESS;
- git diff/scope validation: PASS;
- model calls: 0; live cloud actions: 0.

CI green is supporting evidence only; acceptance is based on the reviewed causal boundary, implementation behavior and preserved evidence contracts.

## Residuals carried forward

PT-3 does not resolve or weaken these mandatory PT-4 inputs:
- persisted quality UNKNOWN can currently coexist with project/API/frontend completed-analysis presentation;
- the original case-02 >7-minute censored observation contradicts unconditional 1-3 minute waiting guidance;
- processing completion and semantic trust must remain separate concepts.

## Merge boundary

PR #247 is accepted for merge. This review does not itself authorize merge, PT-4 implementation, a new live/model evaluation, or teardown. After explicit USER merge, the Product Trust Goal may select the next repository-eligible phase under the Program contract.
